#!RuleTest
#test CDISC-CG0412 expect=violation domain=DM
#note "Authority: SDTM and SDTMIG Conformance Rules v2.0 CG0412 (SDTMIG 3.2; Condition DM.ACTARMCD not in (SCRNFAIL, NOTASSGN, NOTTRT); Rule: subject records in DS > 0). The Check compares upper(ACTARMCD) with the exemption literals: that case-folding is the RULED idiom (PLAN-port-core-expression-improvements Q1(a), owner 2026-09-22; applied to this rule by CHANGE-arm-upper-alignment.tsv), not a Partially Executable limitation. The rule is Partially Executable (underreporting), but the gap between the authority text and the Check is not identified from the text; no row here is chosen to pin one. Subject 01-701-1023 (ACTARMCD=XANHI, not exempt) has no DS record -> row 2 fires. Row 1 has a DS record; row 3 (SCRNFAIL) is exempt by the Condition. ALSO THE S3 DISCRIMINATOR (SKELETON-distinct-function hazard 3): USUBJID in distinct(USUBJID, domain=DS) belongs to the FOREIGN dataset DS; a port that read USUBJID from the primary DM would find every subject in its own set and fall silent."
#library standard=sdtmig version=3-2
#expectViolationCount 1
#expectViolationAt row=2 USUBJID=01-701-1023 ACTARMCD=XANHI
dataset DM label="Demographics"
col STUDYID  type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col DOMAIN   type=Char label="Domain Abbreviation"
col USUBJID  type=Char label="Unique Subject Identifier"
col ARMCD    type=Char label="Planned Arm Code"
col ACTARMCD type=Char label="Actual Arm Code"
---
CDISCPILOT01 | DM | 01-701-1015 | PBO      | PBO
CDISCPILOT01 | DM | 01-701-1023 | XANHI    | XANHI
CDISCPILOT01 | DM | 01-701-1028 | SCRNFAIL | SCRNFAIL
---

dataset DS label="Disposition"
col STUDYID type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col DOMAIN  type=Char label="Domain Abbreviation"
col USUBJID type=Char label="Unique Subject Identifier"
col DSSEQ   type=Num  label="Sequence Number"
col DSTERM  type=Char label="Reported Term for the Disposition Event"
col DSDECOD type=Char label="Standardized Disposition Term"
---
CDISCPILOT01 | DS | 01-701-1015 | 1 | COMPLETED | COMPLETED
---
